# AmdUefiFwConfig - parameter reference

Source: `C:\apex_junczhai@amd.com\testflows\public\amd_uefi_fw_config.html`

`kind` legend: **enum** fixed value domain / **text** free text or number / **server-populated** filled by the APEX server, resolve at build time / **runtime-injected** written by APEX itself, never generate it / **hidden-const** not shown in the dialog.

`origin` legend: blank keeps the APEX flow default / **PMM** a constant this team always overrides / **SLOT** resolved per run, see the checklist below / APEX injected by APEX itself.

## Slots to resolve (1)

These are **not** in the template. A required slot is omitted rather than filled with a placeholder, and the build refuses to emit JSON until it is supplied. If the route below cannot be resolved for the station under test, raise a clarification - do not carry the Example value over.

### `AMD UEFI FW Config (AFC).afcarguments` (required)

- **Route**: An unbounded free-text field, passed through verbatim to `fw_config` on the SUT. THERE IS NO ENUMERABLE DOMAIN and there never will be one: the value can name any BIOS/CBS token the platform exposes, or a path to a settings .txt file, so it cannot be reduced to a dropdown. Do not try to publish a value list - derive the value, and use the examples below only to recognise the shape. The flow's own form ships six examples and a reference page, which are the authoritative mode list: `-p` print every setting to the log; `-p > cmos_settings.txt` store current settings to a file; `-f c:\cmos_settings\cmos_settings.txt` load settings from a file on the APEX Host or the SUT; `-m AMDPBS.AMDPBSOption.SpecialDisplayFeatures=0x4` load a space-separated list of settings from the command line; `-v` print version; `-h` print help. Reference: https://amd.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/BIOSC/pages/613839006/AMD+UEFI+FW+Config+AFC . Three of the six do real work and the flow treats each differently. (1) `-m <TOKEN>=<value> [<TOKEN>=<value> ...]` - tokens in AMD dotted form, AMDCBS.* and AMDPBS.* both legal; this is the mode to use when the case names specific options. (2) `-f <path>` - the flow resolves the path on the Host or file share first, copies it to the SUT AFC directory and rewrites the argument to the bare file name, and falls back to treating it as an SUT-local path. The path MUST NOT contain a space - the flow parses it with `split("-f")[-1].strip().split(" ")[0]`, which truncates at the first space with no error. (3) `-p > <file>` - the redirect is executed by the SUT shell and the flow then copies that file back into the run's result directory; bare `-p` prints into testflow.log and produces NO artifact, because the copy-back is gated on the regex `(-p)\s*>`. `-v` and `-h` are diagnostics with no place in a queue item. Token names and legal values come from the platform's BIOS/CBS definition, not from this skill - look them up, do not copy a token from another program's item.
- **Example**: `-m AMDCBS.SMUCommonOptions.SystemConfiguration=0x01` (select cTDP configuration index 1 on Medusa) - captured on 2026-09-13. Illustrative, not authoritative.
- **Scope of that example**: mode (1) with a single token, and nothing more - it is one observed value, not a recommended default. The same queue also shows mode (1) with two tokens (`...SystemConfiguration=0x0F AMDCBS.SMUDebugOptions.SMUFeatures.P3T=0x01`), mode (2) as `-f \\<fileshare>\share\<user>\Tool\AFC\Settings\<Program>\ACDC_DC.txt`, and mode (3) as `-p > cmos_settings.txt`. The observed `-f` paths are one operator's personal share and are environment-bound (P-009) - resolve the share and the per-program settings file for the station under test, never carry that path across.
- **If unresolved**: clarify with the case owner. There is no safe default: the flow's own default is `-p > cmos_settings.txt`, which reads settings and changes nothing, so an unresolved slot left at the default produces an item that passes while configuring nothing.

## Open questions

- Is `--onfailure=Continue` right for a flow that configures BIOS? It is the form default and is unanimous across all 23 items, so by P-002 it is inheritance and not a recorded team decision. The concrete risk is reachable: on a failed apply the flow raises AFC_EXECUTION_ERROR (98) and, under Continue, the queue proceeds - every downstream item then runs at the previous BIOS configuration and can still report Pass. Whether PMM wants Stop here is a decision for the queue owner; it has not been made, and this file must not manufacture one.
- The `False` half of `rebootafterexecution` has not been observed in a run artifact. Every AFC `testflowArguments.json` found on the Host carries `true`. The type is confirmed boolean, so the flow's truthiness test `self.args.get('rebootafterexecution')` behaves correctly on `false` - but that is read from the conversion rule and the source, not from a `false` run. Now that the policy is unconditional True, this can only be settled from one of the three non-conforming items.
- Should the three AFC-print_settings items in queue 08 be corrected to True? That is a write to a production queue and is out of this skill's read-only scope. Raised, not actioned.

